        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 875,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 807,
        "paragraph_id": "1E27C59E",
        "text": "Due to sediment fluxes"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 33232,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 876,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 808,
        "paragraph_id": "76D4F039",
        "text": "Based on the gradients in the sediment transport the bed level changes according to:"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 33353,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 880,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 812,
        "paragraph_id": "6BAC6474",
        "text": "In (2.110) ρ is the porosity, fmor (keyword: morfac) is a morphological acceleration factor of O(1-10) (Reniers et al., 2004) and qx and qy represent the sediment transport rates in x- and y-direction respectively. Sediment transport can be activated with the keyword: sedtrans."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 33497,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 882,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 814,
        "paragraph_id": "60BC23B9",
        "text": "The morphological acceleration factor speeds up the morphological time scale relative to the hydrodynamic timescale. It means that if you have a simulation of 10 minutes with a morfac of 6 you effectively simulate the morphological evolution over one hour. There are now two ways in which you can input the time-varying parameters in combination with morfac:"
      }
    ],
    "table_cell": null,
    "text_method": "Saved display-field substitution plus w:t; equation objects are not transcribed."
